---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ADS_ENABLED, SITE, SOCIALS } from '../consts';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';

// Bump this whenever the disclosures below change.
const LAST_UPDATED = new Date('2026-11-01T00:00:00Z');
const updated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
}).format(LAST_UPDATED);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description={`What ${SITE.title} collects, what it does not, and which third parties see anything.`}
  path="/privacy"
  narrow
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="page-sub">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="summary">
    <p class="summary__title">The short version</p>
    {
      ADS_ENABLED ? (
        <p>
          This is a static blog. There are no accounts and no comments. The site uses a
          cookieless analytics service, and it shows ads served by Google, which may set cookies
          or use identifiers on your device. You can decline personalized ads. Details are
          below.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          This is a static blog. There are no accounts, no cookies, no advertising and no
          cross-site tracking. Two parties see anything when you load a page: a privacy-focused
          analytics service that records an anonymous page view, and GitHub, which serves the
          files and logs your IP for security. Nothing else is fetched from a third party, and
          that includes fonts. I may add advertising later; the Advertising section says what
          would change.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>

  <div class="prose policy">
    <h2>What is collected</h2>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      This site uses <a href="https://umami.is" rel="noopener">Umami</a>, a cookieless analytics
      service, to count page views. Per its documentation it records{' '}
      <strong>page views, referrer URLs, browser, operating system, device type and country of
      origin</strong>, uses no cookies in its tracking code, collects no personally identifiable
      information and anonymises what it does collect. It does not track you across other websites.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no way for me to identify an individual reader from this data, and I do not try to.
      What I look at is which posts get read and where readers arrive from.
    </p>

    <h3>Server logs</h3>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub's documentation states plainly that when a GitHub
      Pages site is visited, "the visitor's IP address is logged and stored for security purposes,
      regardless of whether the visitor has signed into GitHub or not." That logging is GitHub's,
      not mine, and I have no access to it. It is governed by the{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">
        GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Fonts</h3>
    <p>
      The Inter and JetBrains Mono typefaces are served from this site, not from a font CDN. They
      are downloaded once when the site is built and shipped alongside the pages, so loading a page
      sends nothing to Google or anyone else in order to render text.
    </p>

    <h3>Search</h3>
    <p>
      The <a href={withBase('/search')}>search page</a> runs{' '}
      <a href="https://pagefind.app" rel="noopener">Pagefind</a> entirely in your browser against a
      static index downloaded with the page. Your queries are never sent to a server and are not
      recorded anywhere.
    </p>

    <h3>Theme preference</h3>
    <p>
      Choosing light or dark mode stores a single value, <code>theme</code>, in your browser's{' '}
      <code>localStorage</code>. It never leaves your device, is not readable by anyone else, and is
      not a cookie. Clearing your site data removes it, and the site then follows your operating
      system's preference.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    {
      ADS_ENABLED ? (
        <>
          <p>
            This site shows ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may place and
            read cookies in your browser, or use web beacons, IP addresses and other identifiers,
            to serve ads and to measure them. Those ads can be based on your visits to this site
            and to other sites. I do not receive that data, and I cannot see which ads any
            individual reader was shown.
          </p>
          <p>
            Google explains how it uses information from sites like this one in its{' '}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
              partner sites policy</a>. You can turn off personalized advertising in{' '}
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google's ad settings</a>, or
            use <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> to opt out of
            personalized ads from participating companies.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, a
            consent banner asks before personalized ads are shown. If you decline, you see
            non-personalized ads only.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>
          This site does not show ads today and loads no advertising code. I may apply for
          Google AdSense in the future. If that happens, this page will be updated before any ad
          appears. It will say that Google and its partners may place cookies or use identifiers
          to serve and measure ads, link to Google's controls for personalized advertising, and
          describe the consent choice shown to readers in the European Economic Area, the United
          Kingdom and Switzerland.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>What is not collected</h2>
    <ul>
      {!ADS_ENABLED && <li>No cookies are set by this site.</li>}
      {!ADS_ENABLED && <li>No advertising, ad networks or advertising identifiers.</li>}
      <li>
        No tracking of my own across other sites or devices, and no fingerprinting.
        {ADS_ENABLED && ' Advertising is covered in the section above.'}
      </li>
      <li>No accounts, sign-ups, comments or newsletter, so there is nothing to submit.</li>
      <li>No email addresses or contact details are collected anywhere on this site.</li>
      <li>
        {ADS_ENABLED ? 'I do not sell data and I do not pass it to data brokers.' : 'Nothing is sold or shared with data brokers.'}
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Posts link out to documentation, papers and source repositories. Following one of those links
      takes you to a site with its own privacy practices, which I have no control over and do not
      vouch for.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data rights</h2>
    <p>
      Because nothing I collect identifies you, there is no personal record for me to look up,
      export or delete. {ADS_ENABLED && 'Data that Google collects for ads is governed by its own policies and controls, linked above. '}If you have a question about any of this, or think something on this page is
      inaccurate, the fastest route is to open an issue on the{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/sehyunnoh/techblog" rel="noopener">site's repository</a> or reach
      me on {SOCIALS.map((s, i) => (
        <>{i > 0 ? ' or ' : ''}<a href={s.href} rel="noopener">{s.label}</a></>
      ))}.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If what this site collects changes, this page changes with it and the date at the top is
      updated. The page lives in the site's public{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/sehyunnoh/techblog/commits/main/src/pages/privacy.astro" rel="noopener">
        Git history</a>, so every revision is visible.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    font-weight: 680;
  }

  .page-sub {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.75rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .summary {
    padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .summary__title {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 620;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
  }

  .summary p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .policy {
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* The first heading sits right under the summary card, so drop the rule. */
  .policy :global(h2:first-of-type) {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }
</style>
